'''''Pla dels Pins, Cumará, Estret''''' is a municipality in the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 35,968 in 2026, it is a semi-rural suburb in the western part of the comarca, characterised by low-density housing and extensive open land. The municipality's name ({{lang|ca|pla dels pins}}, "plain of pines") refers to the pine groves that historically covered the area, remnants of which survive in the eastern uplands.

== Geography ==

Pla dels Pins occupies a broad, flat plain in western Cumará, between the coastal strip of [[Costa Serena]] and the inland foothills. The terrain is predominantly level, with elevations ranging from 40 to 100 metres. The eastern edge of the municipality rises into the foothills of the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] range, where remnant pine forests persist. Several small streams drain westward across the plain toward the coast.

=== Climate ===

Pla dels Pins has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} ({{w|Köppen climate classification|Köppen}} Am), with average daily highs of 30 to 32 °C and lows of 22 to 24 °C. Annual precipitation averages approximately 2,200 to 2,500 mm, with the wet season from May to November.

== Demographics ==

Pla dels Pins's population of 35,968 is dispersed across low-density residential developments and scattered farmsteads. The population is predominantly [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboan]] and mixed Balboan, with a small [[Fosian Balboan|Fosian]] community. The municipality has experienced slow population growth, as its distance from major transit corridors and lack of dense residential development have limited its attractiveness to speculative construction.

== Economy ==

The economy of Pla dels Pins is based on small-scale agriculture and residential services. The fertile plain supports the cultivation of maize, vegetables, and fruit, though agricultural output is modest compared to the more intensive farming operations in [[Brises, Estret|Brises]] and [[Els Camps, Estret|Els Camps]]. A limited range of local retail and service businesses operates in the residential areas. Some residents commute to [[Costa Serena]] or [[Sant Cristòfor]] for employment.

== Transport ==

Pla dels Pins is connected to the surrounding municipalities by local roads. The municipality does not have a CristoCarril rail station; the nearest rail access is at [[Costa Serena (CristoCarril)|Costa Serena]] on [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] to the west or [[La Cruïlla (CristoCarril)|La Cruïlla]] to the east. The [[E68 expressway (Balboa)|E68 expressway]] passes near the municipality, providing a road link to the E5 corridor.

